# Redirects for this Worker's static assets.
#
# Deliberately empty of rules. This project deploys as a Worker with static
# assets (`wrangler deploy`), which serves exactly one hostname per deployment
# and only accepts relative paths here — it rejected the apex-to-www rule that
# used to live in this file, because the source was an absolute URL
# (https://peacemakerbrewster.com/*) and the parser doesn't support the "301!"
# force suffix either.
#
# The apex->www canonicalisation still needs to happen, just one layer up: a
# zone-level Redirect Rule (Cloudflare dashboard → Rules → Redirect Rules),
# which runs before traffic ever reaches this Worker and works regardless of
# what's behind it. See DEPLOY.md.
#
# If a same-host, path-only redirect is ever needed (e.g. an old URL that
# moved), the working syntax here is:
#   /old-path  /new-path  301
